H2: Known Faults - Fiat 500X
H3: Electrical Faults and Warning Lights
P: MONITOR ú Some cars ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says faults with the electrical system were a common concern, with warning lights and infotainment glitches frequently mentioned.
P: Parkers says its owners' reviews show no common faults of concern. A few owners report electrical systems have gone wrong, but Parkers says these seem to be isolated incidents.
P: A Carbuyer owner review describes an engine fault light coming on after a drive in heavy rain, with the automatic stop/start not working and the dashboard display losing the date and time. A few days later the warning came on again, this time with an electronic parking brake fault.
H3: Locks and Windows
P: MINOR ú Some cars ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says owners report problems with locks, windows and other such items.
H3: Uconnect Bluetooth
P: MINOR ú Some cars ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says the Uconnect system can drop a phone's Bluetooth connection. It adds that this isn't specific to one make and reportedly happens with all brands.
H3: Diesel Engine Management
P: MONITOR ú Diesel ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says some diesel owners reported problems with the engine management system, which led to expensive repairs outside of warranty.
H3: Automatic Gearbox
P: MINOR ú Some cars ú Get a quote
P: Carwow says the standard automatic gearbox on the quicker petrol model is frustratingly slow to change, which blunts acceleration.
P: Another Carbuyer owner mentions turbo lag and rather jerky gear changes sometimes if accelerating hard.
H3: Fault Returning After a Warranty Fix
P: CHECK ú Some cars ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says one owner noted that a fault reappeared shortly after being fixed under warranty.
H3: Reliability Survey Results
P: MONITOR ú Some cars ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says reliability and build quality have traditionally been a sticking point for Italian cars, and that customer feedback suggests Fiat has a way to go on quality and service.
P: Carbuyer says around 13.8% of customers reported a fault within the first year.
P: What Car? says the 500X didn't get enough responses to finish in its latest Reliability Survey. It adds that the 500X and its Jeep Renegade sister car haven't done particularly well in previous surveys.
P: Parkers says the newer 500X has established itself a good record of dependability.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists several 500X recalls, including these.
LI: Affected vehicles may have been fitted with a faulty 48-volt battery.
LI: The rear right brake calliper could display micro-cracks.
LI: Non-conformity in the airbag control module software.
LI: In case of an accident if the rear seat belts are not fastened i.e. if the rear seat is not occupied by a passenger or is occupied by a child restraint system coupled only to the Isofix anchors and the pretensioners are deployed the rear seat latch could be released.
LI: The transmission could unexpectedly switch to the N position due to a nonconformity in the transmission wiring assembly process.
P: Enter the registration in our recall check to see whether a car has an open recall.
