H2: Known Faults - Fiat Panda
P: The faults below come from What Car?'s reliability reviews of the 2004-2012 and 2012-2024 cars, Autocar's buying guide to the previous generation, Auto Express's used review of the newer car, the RAC, one Carbuyer owner review and DVSA's recall data. Each section names its source.
H3: Clutch
P: MONITOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says that on a few 2004-2012 cars the clutch juddered. It repeats the same note for the 2012-2024 car. Autocar, writing about the previous generation, says shifting woes are more frequently attributed to the hydraulic clutch than the transmission itself. Auto Express says some Mk3 Pandas have suffered from a loud clutch or gearbox, and that it is initially hard to work out which one is noisy. On a test drive, pull away gently and change through the gears while you listen.
H3: Tailgate Release and Boot Lock
P: MINOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says some 2004-2012 Pandas suffered from a jammed tailgate release mechanism, and it gives the same note for the 2012-2024 car. Auto Express tells buyers of the Mk3 to check that the electronically controlled boot lock works as it should, because it sometimes doesn't. Open and close the tailgate several times before you agree a price.
H3: Head Gasket
P: MONITOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: Autocar says head gasket failure is a possibility across the range of the previous-generation Panda. It suggests keeping an eye out for milky oil or white exhaust smoke. It adds that the canniest customers will also look for signs of water ingress and accident damage, particularly on the Panda 4x4. Look at the oil filler cap and watch the exhaust when the engine starts.
H3: Electrics and Warning Lights
P: MONITOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: For the 2012-2024 car, What Car? says there are known problems with engine electrics, with some faults reported in suspension components too. In its reliability survey, several owners reported minor but recurring issues, including warning lights and electrical faults, particularly with infotainment systems and sensors. One owner noted a persistent engine management light that dealers struggled to resolve effectively. Check every warning light comes on and goes out, and try the infotainment screen.
H3: Power and Throttle Response
P: MONITOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says the Euro 6-spec Panda 1.2 can suffer from a lack of power when attempting to pull away. Autocar says that on the previous generation an ECU fault can cause jumpy accelerator response but is usually cured with a software update. Pay attention to how the car pulls away and how the accelerator feels at low speed.
H3: Fuel and Oil Consumption
P: CHECK ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: For the 2004-2012 car, What Car? suggests asking the previous owners about its fuel and oil consumption, as some owners have reported that both are abnormally high. Ask for service records, and look for oil top-ups noted by the seller.
H3: Power Steering
P: CHECK ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: One owner told Carbuyer that the power steering is very expensive to fix because the entire dashboard has to be taken out. That is one owner's experience, not a survey result. Turn the wheel from lock to lock while parked and listen for anything unusual.
H3: Distributor Caps
P: MINOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: The RAC, reviewing the 2004-2012 car, says some owners have reported faulty distributor caps, but that these should all have been replaced under warranty by now. Ask whether the car has had any ignition work.
H3: Safety Recalls
P: CHECK ú Any miles ú Ask a Fiat dealer
P: DVSA's recall data lists several Panda recalls, including these.
LI: On affected vehicles the reversing gear switch is not according to specification.
LI: Affected vehicles fitted with the side airbag/head airbag may not have the side crash sensor connected correctly which may in a worst-case scenario result in non-deployment of the airbag in a side impact/crash.
LI: The steering column height adjustment mechanism could accidentally release.
LI: Some vehicles were assembled without the engine suspension reaction bracket fitted on the transmission side.
LI: It has been identified that due to a nonconformity in the transmission casing mount material there is a possibility that the casting may fail.
LI: In some circumstances the headlights can switch off without warning which will increase the risk of an accident.
LI: It has been identified that the front seatbelt anchorage links may not have been manufactured to the correct specification.
LI: The upper fork on the steering shaft fork may not have been correctly fixed/'staked' onto the shaft.
LI: There is a possibility of a short circuit in the ABS control unit due to infiltration of chemical solutions.
LI: Fuel delivery pipe adjacent to air filter may chafe.
P: DVSA lists these simply as "PANDA", so the data doesn't say which year or generation each one covers. Enter the registration in our recall check to see whether a particular car has work outstanding.
H2: Buying a used Fiat Panda
P: For the 2004-2012 car, What Car? cites Warranty Direct as saying very few faults have been reported by owners, and the RAC says the Panda has thus far proved relatively reliable. For the 2012-2024 car, What Car? says owners had a mixed experience with reliability and dealer support. Auto Express says the Mk3 has slowly slipped down the charts since its debut in 2014, and that it ranked 128th in its 2016 Driver Power survey.
P: The RAC says to check for off-road damage on the 4x4 and for parking knocks and scrapes on the others. Auto Express says it is not unusual for the Panda's dashboard to rattle.
P: Before you buy, drive the car with the radio off. Listen to the clutch and gearbox, try the tailgate, and look at the dashboard for warning lights. Then ask to see proof that any recall work was completed. For job prices and engine details, see our Fiat Panda parts guide .
H2: Breakdown cover
P: If a fault stops the car on the road, breakdown cover sends help to you. Compare two UK providers and check what each policy includes.
P: We earn a commission if you buy cover through these links, at no cost to you ( how we're paid ).
