H2: Frequently asked questions
P: For the 2004-2012 Panda, What Car? cites Warranty Direct as saying very few faults had been reported by owners, and the RAC called that car relatively reliable. For the 2012-2024 car, What Car? says owners had a mixed experience with reliability and dealer support, and Auto Express reported it ranked 128th in its 2016 Driver Power survey.
P: What Car? mentions clutch judder and a jammed tailgate release on the 2004-2012 car, and engine electrics and suspension faults on the 2012-2024 car. Autocar says head gasket failure is a possibility on the previous generation, and Auto Express lists a loud clutch or gearbox and a boot lock that sometimes does not work on the newer one.
P: Yes. DVSA&#39;s recall data lists several Panda recalls, covering things such as the reversing gear switch, side crash sensors, the steering column height adjustment and the headlights. Enter the registration in our [recall check](/car-recall-check) to see whether a particular car has work outstanding.
P: Test the clutch and listen for noise from the clutch or gearbox. Look for milky oil or white exhaust smoke, check the tailgate release and boot lock, and watch the dashboard for warning lights. Ask the seller to show that recall work was done.
