H2: Known Faults - Fiat Tipo
H3: Uconnect Touchscreen and Infotainment
P: MONITOR ú 2016-2020 cars ú Get a quote
P: In its review of the Tipo (2016 - 2020), RAC says a bigger issue is the restricted size of the 'Uconnect' infotainment touchscreen in the centre of the dash.
P: RAC also says the technology behind the infotainment system wasn't stellar, and advises making sure that everything works as it should and connects to your phone.
H3: Build Quality and Interior Materials
P: MINOR ú 2016 onwards cars ú Get a quote
P: RAC says build quality wasn't stellar. Auto Express, in its used review of the Tipo Mk2 (2016-date), describes the cabin as sober and functional, with impressive build quality but a combination of high-quality and cheap materials.
P: Parkers adds that some aspects of the interior don't feel particularly well made.
H3: Diesel Emissions System Components
P: MONITOR ú 2016-2023 hatchback ú Get a quote
P: Parkers, writing about the Tipo hatchback (2016 - 2023), says that on the whole there are no particular reliability concerns beyond the usual diesel emissions system components that need replacement with age.
H3: Only One Remote Key
P: CHECK ú 2016 onwards cars ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express normally recommends getting both remote keys with a used car, but says the Tipo came with only one.
H3: Space-Saver Spare on the Hatchback
P: MINOR ú 2016 onwards cars ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says the Tipo hatch gets a space saver spare wheel, but if you buy a Tipo estate you get a full-sized wheel.
H3: What Car? Reliability Survey and Fiat
P: MONITOR ú Fiat as a brand ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says the Tipo is quite new, which is why it did not feature in its latest Reliability Survey.
P: It adds that Fiat, as a brand, didn't do particularly well, and that the manufacturer came in 24th place out of 32 car brands.
H3: Driver Power Surveys and Fiat
P: MINOR ú Fiat as a brand ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express says that as the Tipo sells in relatively low numbers, it doesn't tend to appear in its Driver Power survey. It reports that Fiat finished a credible 15th out of 30 manufacturers in 2019, with reliability, an historical Fiat bugbear, now one of the higher rated aspects of Fiat ownership, and that Fiat's reputation for reliability has improved in recent years.
P: Carbuyer stresses that its feedback applies to Fiat cars on the whole, because too few Tipo owners took part for the model to be featured individually. It says a 15th-place finish in its 2019 Driver Power owner satisfaction survey was the strongest showing Fiat has had in recent years, but that Fiat couldn't replicate that result in the past couple of years.
H3: Testers' Views on Durability
P: MINOR ú 2016-2023 cars ú Get a quote
P: Carbuyer says the Tipo Station Wagon (2016-2021) feels built to last, while its relative mechanical simplicity should help dependability.
H3: Reliable Lounge 1.6 MultiJet, One Owner's Report
P: CHECK ú One owner's report ú Get a quote
P: One Parkers owner of a Lounge 1.6 MultiJet II five-door wrote that it has been completely reliable for them, that it handles the motorway very well, and that they have had absolutely no problems with it.
P: Run a registration through our recall check before you buy, and read the Fiat Tipo parts page for the engines testers describe.
