H2: Known Faults - Fiat Ducato
H3: Battery Drain (Alarm Module)
P: MONITOR ú 2007 on ú Get a quote
P: CAT Magazine says an unexplained battery drain is often due to an alarm module under the seat shorting out due to water ingress.
H3: Central Locking
P: MONITOR ú 2007 on ú Get a quote
P: CAT Magazine says that if the central locking fails, it is probably due to the module under the facia.
H3: Temperature Readings (Instrument Cluster and Loom)
P: MONITOR ú 2007 on ú Get a quote
P: For strange temperature readings, CAT Magazine says the cause is not the temperature sensor (as is often thought) but dry solder joints on the instrument cluster. It describes another fault that leads the driver to think their van is losing its cool, down to a corroded part of the loom. It says the routing of the loom around the pedal box apparently causes the problem, so chafed or broken wires could be the root cause.
H3: EGR Valve
P: MONITOR ú 2007 on ú Get a quote
P: CAT Magazine says engine hesitation, failure to start and irregular idle speeds can be attributed to a faulty EGR valve.
H3: Steering Rack, Top Mounts and Ball Joints
P: MONITOR ú 2007 on ú Get a quote
P: CAT Magazine says the lack of lubrication and excessive levels of strain can lead to premature damage to the steering rack. It says the top strut mounting and bearings can fail regularly, causing the steering to become tight. It also says the high centre of gravity, coupled with the use a van gets, can cause premature wear of the ball joint.
H3: Peeling Silver Paint
P: MINOR ú 2007 on ú Get a quote
P: CAT Magazine says silver paint, as used on the Ducato, has an odd tendency to peel off.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists several Ducato recalls, including these.
LI: Certain kinds of vehicle acceleration could cause the speed limiter to turn off.
LI: Due to a nonconformity in production the side marker lights are not functioning.
LI: The third (high level) brake light may not function.
P: Put a Ducato's registration into our recall check to find out whether it has an open recall.
H2: Reliability Reports
P: Parkers says it is not unusual to find people complaining about the reliability of older Fiat Ducatos, and that this generation seems to have few recurring problems.
P: The RAC's review of the 2011-2014 Ducato says it has earned a decent reliability record, helped in no small part by its rugged diesel engines. It adds that there has never been a great deal of criticism about the Fiat's reliability or sheer utility.
P: Van Reviewer says reliability has improved, and so has dealer support and coverage.
H2: Warranty
P: Fiat Professional UK says its warranty is limited to 60k miles (100k miles on commercial vehicles) in the third year, with unlimited mileage before that.
P: Parkers says you can pay extra for an extended warranty that stretches cover to 125,000 miles.
