H2: Frequently asked questions
P: The RAC says the 2010-2014 Doblo has earned a decent reliability record, helped by its reliable engines. For the 2010-2022 Cargo van it says the build quality is quite stout and most problems are minor. Parkers says the 2001-2010 Doblo seems to have fared well despite Fiat&#39;s reputation.
P: The RAC reports gearbox complaints and failing headlamps on the 2015-2019 car, and warns about the Dualogic semi-automatic. Parkers mentions wiper issues, a plastic part in the rear central locking and minor earthing faults on the Cargo van. Owner reviews add brake, gearbox and electrical complaints, each from one owner.
P: Yes. DVSA&#39;s recall data lists several Doblo recalls, including a brake vacuum pump fault, a diesel fuel return pipe and the anti-roll bar. Put the registration through our [recall check](/car-recall-check) to see what applies to a particular vehicle.
P: For the 2010-2014 Doblo the RAC suggests checking for child-seat upholstery damage, dints and scrapes, slipping clutches on manual cars and that every electrical function works. For the Cargo van it advises looking out for slow starting, tapping from the engine bay and dark exhaust smoke.
