H2: Known Faults - Fiat Scudo
P: The notes below come from the RAC, Parkers, Auto Express and DVSA.
H3: Steering Rack and Steering Arms
P: MONITOR ú 2007-2016 ú Get a quote
P: In its 2007-2016 Scudo review the RAC says that if the mileage is approaching 70,000, the steering rack may need repairing. It adds that if the work is not done, the van will end up with excessive play in the steering arms, which could lead to an MoT test failure.
H3: Suspension Knocking Over Bumps
P: MONITOR ú 2007-2016 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says that a knocking sound from the suspension over speed bumps means a bottom ball joint may need swapping.
H3: Differential Noise
P: MONITOR ú 2007-2016 ú Get a quote
P: According to the RAC, a droning or whirring noise on the 2007-2016 van is a sign that the differential needs replacing.
H3: Exhaust
P: CHECK ú 2007-2016 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says the exhaust on the 2007-2016 Scudo is expensive to replace. Its advice for the test drive is to start the engine from cold with the cab door open and listen for any odd exhaust noises.
H3: Sliding Side Doors
P: CHECK ú 2007-2016 ú Get a quote
P: The RAC tells buyers to ensure the sliding side doors slide cleanly down the full length of their runners. If they do not, it says, the runners may have to be replaced.
H3: Power Steering Pump
P: MONITOR ú 2007-2016 ú Get a quote
P: Auto Express reports power steering problems on the 2007-2016 Scudo, which could result in replacement of the power-steering pump.
H3: Clutch
P: MINOR ú 2007-2016 ú Get a quote
P: Parkers says its testers often found themselves stalling or wheel-spinning once the clutch bites on the 2007-2016 van, but adds that it would recommend it if you need to cover distance or carry heavy loads.
H3: Engine Reliability
P: MINOR ú Any miles ú Get a quote
P: Parkers says the engines of the 2007-2016 Scudo tend to be reliable, and Auto Express says they have a good reputation for reliability and the ability to cover many trouble-free miles. For the 1996-2006 van, Parkers calls each of the two engines legendary for longevity as long as they have been maintained properly.
P: Auto Express says the engines in the current van are tried-and-tested units and should be as reliable as any other diesel commercial vehicle. Parkers says the electric E-Scudo has identical versions on sale for long enough that any problems with its electric powertrain would have become well known, and that those vans have been reliable so far.
H3: Safety Recalls
P: CHECK ú Any age ú Ask a Fiat dealer
P: DVSA's recall data lists many Scudo recalls, including these.
LI: On affected vehicles a non-conformity issue with the fuel injection common rail may lead to a loosening of the nut and a potential fuel leak.
LI: Affected vehicles may have been equipped with the incorrect rear springs, which can impair driving behaviour when fully loaded or risk the rear spring detaching when empty.
LI: On the affected vehicle the tightening torque applied to the steering rack during production may be insufficient.
LI: Vehicles may have been fitted with the front crossmember incorrectly tightened.
LI: In a significant frontal collision the driver's airbag may not deploy correctly, due to a non-conformity in the supplier's production process.
LI: The fuel return pipe connector at the injectors may wear over time and leak.
LI: On certain vehicles the front brake discs may not be the required thickness for the vehicle definition.
LI: Vehicles fitted with rear brake drums may suffer contamination of the brake lining.
H2: Buying a used Fiat Scudo
P: Enter the registration in our recall check before you buy. For estimates on brakes, clutch, battery and services, see our Fiat Scudo parts guide .
