P: Parkers says the engines of the 2007-2016 Scudo tend to be reliable, and Auto Express says they earned a good reputation for reliability and the ability to cover many trouble-free miles. For the 1996-2006 van Parkers calls each of the two engines legendary for longevity, as long as they have been maintained properly.
P: For the 2007-2016 van the RAC lists a steering rack that may need repairing, a knocking bottom ball joint, a differential that needs replacing when it drones or whirrs, an expensive exhaust and sliding side doors that must run cleanly on their runners. Auto Express reports power steering problems that could lead to a new pump.
P: Yes. DVSA&#39;s recall data lists many Scudo recalls, among them a fuel injection common rail nut, the rear springs, the steering rack tightening torque and the front crossmember. Put the registration through our [recall check](/car-recall-check) to see what applies to a particular van.
P: For the 2007-2016 van the RAC says to start the engine from cold with the cab door open and listen for any odd exhaust noises. It also says to make sure the sliding side doors slide cleanly down the full length of their runners, because otherwise the runners may have to be replaced.
